# Security Patterns

Apply when working on login, admin routes, JWT, or user-generated content.

## Authentication Flow

- Client: JWT in `localStorage`, attached via `client/src/api/axiosConfig.js`
- Server: issued in `adminController.js`, verified by `server/src/middleware/auth.js`
- Admin UI guard is client-side only — server does not yet enforce role checks

## When Touching Auth

- Preserve 401 interceptor behavior in `axiosConfig.js`
- Consider adding role-check middleware for `/api/admin/*` and blog write routes
- Keep rate limiters on login, comments, and AI endpoints — extend, do not remove
- Hash passwords via existing Mongoose pre-save hook in `User.js`

## Input Handling

- Sanitize rendered HTML with DOMPurify on the client
- Validate user input in `server/src/validators/` before controllers run
- Consider wiring `express-mongo-sanitize` in `server.js` for NoSQL injection protection

## Environment & Secrets

- Never commit `.env` files — only update `.env.example` with placeholder values
- Keep env vars in sync across `.env.example`, `docker-compose.yml`, and `init-scripts/`
- Do not hardcode secrets, tokens, or passwords in source code or rules files
- Reference seed credentials only in local `.env.example` / README, never in shared AI rules

## Do Not

- Assume server enforces admin role on protected routes
- Log or expose passwords, tokens, or connection strings
- Remove security middleware (Helmet, rate limiters, CORS config) without replacement
